.TH SOVR-CLI "1" "August 2026" "Soveroot experimental RPC client" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sovr-cli \- communicate with an experimental Soveroot node
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sovr-cli
.B \-chain=labnet
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ parameters ]
.PP
.B sovr-cli
.B \-chain=labnet \-named
.I command
.RI [ name=value ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sovr-cli
sends JSON-RPC commands to a running
.BR sovrd (1)
process.
.PP
This experimental client is restricted to the isolated, non-production
.BR labnet .
Select it explicitly with
.BR \-chain=labnet .
The client rejects inherited Bitcoin mainnet, testnet, signet, and regtest
selection so that the Soveroot-branded client cannot accidentally control an
inherited-network node. Labnet coins have no monetary value.
.PP
Run
.B sovr-cli \-help
for the complete client option list, or
.B sovr-cli \-chain=labnet help
for the RPC command list exposed by the running node.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-chain=labnet
Select the only network permitted by the application isolation interlock.
.TP
.B \-named
Pass RPC parameters as
.I name=value
pairs instead of positional arguments.
.TP
.B \-rpcconnect=HOST
Connect to the RPC server at HOST. The default is 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.B \-rpcport=PORT
Connect to PORT. Labnet's provisional RPC default is 29443.
.TP
.B \-rpcwallet=NAME
Send the command to the named wallet endpoint.
.TP
.B \-rpcwait
Wait for the RPC server to become available.
.TP
.B \-help
Print the complete, build-specific client help and exit.
.TP
.B \-version
Print version and licensing information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show labnet chain information:
.PP
.EX
sovr-cli -chain=labnet getblockchaininfo
.EE
.PP
List loaded wallets:
.PP
.EX
sovr-cli -chain=labnet listwallets
.EE
.PP
Call an RPC with named parameters:
.PP
.EX
sovr-cli -chain=labnet -named getblockhash height=1
.EE
.SH SAFETY
Soveroot is experimental software. This repository does not provide a live
monetary network, production release, token sale, or security guarantee. Do not
use labnet wallets or keys to protect assets of value.
